§ `Time Definitions and Helpers`

-- TIME is a wall-clock time-of-day. No date, no timezone.
-- Uses 24-hour format internally. Hours 0-23, minutes 0-59, seconds 0-59.

§§ `Constants`

@nlg the number of seconds in a minute
`Seconds in a minute` MEANS 60
@nlg the number of minutes in an hour
`Minutes in an hour`  MEANS 60
@nlg the number of hours in a day
`Hours in a day`      MEANS 24
@nlg the number of seconds in an hour
`Seconds in an hour`  MEANS 3600
@nlg the number of seconds in a day
`Seconds in a day`    MEANS 86400

@nlg midnight at the start of the day
DECIDE Midnight IS TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0

@nlg noon
DECIDE Noon IS TIME_FROM_HMS 12 0 0


§§ `Meridiem`

DECLARE `Meridiem Indicator` IS ONE OF am, pm

§§ `Time Constructors`

-- Time h m s  (3 NUMBERs -> TIME)
GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %h% hours, %m% minutes and %s% seconds
`Time` MEANS
    TIME_FROM_HMS h m s

-- Time h m  (2 NUMBERs -> TIME, seconds=0)
GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %h% hours and %m% minutes
`Time` MEANS
    TIME_FROM_HMS h m 0

-- Time h  (1 NUMBER -> TIME, minutes=0, seconds=0)
GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %h% hours
`Time` MEANS
    TIME_FROM_HMS h 0 0

-- Time t  (identity: 1 TIME -> TIME)
GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg %t%
`Time` MEANS t

-- Time str  -> parse time string (HH:MM:SS, HH:MM)
GIVEN str IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE TIME
@nlg the time in %str%, if it can be read
`Time` MEANS TOTIME str

-- Time dt  -> extract time from DATETIME (ignores date and timezone)
GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time of %dt% in its own time zone
`Time` MEANS DATETIME_TIME dt

-- Time h m s am/pm  (3 NUMBERs + Meridiem Indicator -> TIME)
GIVEN h  IS A NUMBER
      m  IS A NUMBER
      s  IS A NUMBER
      ap IS A `Meridiem Indicator`
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %m% minutes and %s% seconds past %h% o'clock %ap%
`Time` MEANS
    IF ap EQUALS am
    THEN TIME_FROM_HMS (IF h EQUALS 12 THEN 0 ELSE h) m s
    ELSE TIME_FROM_HMS (IF h EQUALS 12 THEN 12 ELSE h PLUS 12) m s

-- Time h m am/pm  (2 NUMBERs + Meridiem Indicator -> TIME)
GIVEN h  IS A NUMBER
      m  IS A NUMBER
      ap IS A `Meridiem Indicator`
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %m% minutes past %h% o'clock %ap%
`Time` MEANS
    Time h m 0 ap

-- Time h am/pm  (1 NUMBER + Meridiem Indicator -> TIME)
GIVEN h  IS A NUMBER
      ap IS A `Meridiem Indicator`
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %h% o'clock %ap%
`Time` MEANS
    Time h 0 0 ap


§§ `Time Extractors`

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the hour of %t% on the 24-hour clock
`the hour of` t MEANS TIME_HOUR t

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the minute of %t%
`the minute of` t MEANS TIME_MINUTE t

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the second of %t%
`the second of` t MEANS TIME_SECOND t


§§ `Time Serial`

-- Serial is fraction of day (0.0 = midnight, 0.5 = noon, 1.0 = next midnight)
GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the fraction of a day elapsed at %t%
t `Time to serial` MEANS TIME_SERIAL t

GIVEN serial IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time at which the fraction %serial% of a day has elapsed
serial `Serial to time` MEANS TIME_FROM_SERIAL serial


§§ `Time Arithmetic`

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% hours after %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `plus hours` n MEANS
    LET serial BE TIME_SERIAL t PLUS (n DIVIDED BY `Hours in a day`)
    IN TIME_FROM_SERIAL (serial MINUS FLOOR serial)

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% minutes after %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `plus minutes` n MEANS
    LET serial BE TIME_SERIAL t PLUS (n DIVIDED BY `Seconds in a day` TIMES `Seconds in a minute`)
    IN TIME_FROM_SERIAL (serial MINUS FLOOR serial)

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% seconds after %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `plus seconds` n MEANS
    LET serial BE TIME_SERIAL t PLUS (n DIVIDED BY `Seconds in a day`)
    IN TIME_FROM_SERIAL (serial MINUS FLOOR serial)

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% hours before %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `minus hours` n MEANS t `plus hours` (0 MINUS n)

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% minutes before %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `minus minutes` n MEANS t `plus minutes` (0 MINUS n)

GIVEN t IS A TIME
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the time %n% seconds before %t% (wrapping past midnight)
t `minus seconds` n MEANS t `plus seconds` (0 MINUS n)


§§ `Time Predicates`

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %t% is before noon
t `is before noon` MEANS TIME_HOUR t LESS THAN 12

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %t% is at or after noon
t `is after noon` MEANS TIME_HOUR t AT LEAST 12

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %t% is in the morning (before noon)
t `is morning` MEANS TIME_HOUR t LESS THAN 12

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %t% is in the afternoon (from noon until 6 pm)
t `is afternoon` MEANS TIME_HOUR t AT LEAST 12 AND TIME_HOUR t LESS THAN 18

GIVEN t IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %t% is in the evening (from 6 pm until midnight)
t `is evening` MEANS TIME_HOUR t AT LEAST 18


§§ `Time Comparators`

GIVEN t1 IS A TIME
      t2 IS A TIME
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the earlier of %t1% and %t2%
`the earlier of` t1 t2 MEANS
    IF TIME_SERIAL t1 AT MOST TIME_SERIAL t2 THEN t1 ELSE t2

GIVEN t1 IS A TIME
      t2 IS A TIME
GIVETH A TIME
@nlg the later of %t1% and %t2%
`the later of` t1 t2 MEANS
    IF TIME_SERIAL t1 AT LEAST TIME_SERIAL t2 THEN t1 ELSE t2


§§ `Native overloads`

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is at or after %b%
`__GEQ__` MEANS
    TIME_SERIAL a AT LEAST TIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is at or before %b%
`__LEQ__` MEANS
    TIME_SERIAL a AT MOST TIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
`__GT__` MEANS
    TIME_SERIAL a GREATER THAN TIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
`__LT__` MEANS
    TIME_SERIAL a LESS THAN TIME_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
a `is before` b MEANS a LESS THAN b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
a `is after` b MEANS a GREATER THAN b

GIVEN a IS A TIME
      b IS A TIME
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of seconds from %b% to %a%
`__MINUS__` MEANS
    (TIME_SERIAL a MINUS TIME_SERIAL b) TIMES `Seconds in a day`
